# Copy to .env.local and fill in. See docs/STAGING_RUNBOOK.md.
# For the LOCAL STAGING stack (supabase start), the values are:

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=          # printed by `supabase start` (anon key)
VITE_MCP_PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1/mcp-server

# R9 · the build's EDITION (docs/EDITIONS_AND_TIERS.md). ABSENT = the community
# (OSS) build — the safe default — which hides every surface whose code the
# community tree does not carry: repo import, Priority chrome, the Team roster.
# Set it to `hosted` when testing the managed product locally, or the hosted-only
# chrome will be invisible however high the account's tier is.
#VITE_NODESPEC_EDITION=hosted

# Owner 2026-09-15: tier-VARIANT testing (Team seats chrome, Enterprise, the
# Government classification banner) is exercised deliberately, one tier at a
# time, under this dev-only flag — it never leaks into ordinary local testing
# and a production build ignores it entirely. Client presentation only; the
# server still resolves the real tier (the runbook's server-side Government
# proof still bumps the seeded subscription row).
#VITE_NODESPEC_TEST_TIER=government

# Cloudflare Turnstile "always passes" test key — fine for staging, never for production.
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
